From: Hummingbird <hummingbird@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Resolve the ^11 uuid ranges to 11.1.0 to avoid a nested uuid 11.1.1

12.4.14's lockfile resolves the ^11 uuid ranges to 11.1.1 while the root and
eight workspaces pin 11.1.0 exactly. Yarn then nests uuid 11.1.1, and its
.bin/uuid symlink, under the elasticsearch plugin. Grafana's test helper
fs.CopyRecursive fails on that symlink, so %check fails. Merging the ^11
ranges into the 11.1.0 entry, as 12.4.13 had, hoists a single uuid.

Lockfile-only change: no package.json edit is needed.

diff --git a/yarn.lock b/yarn.lock
index f26fa1737ae6..1de9ab59d5eb 100644
--- a/yarn.lock
+++ b/yarn.lock
@@ -36021,7 +36021,7 @@ __metadata:
   languageName: node
   linkType: hard
 
-"uuid@npm:11.1.0":
+"uuid@npm:11.1.0, uuid@npm:^11.0.0, uuid@npm:^11.0.5, uuid@npm:^11.1.0":
   version: 11.1.0
   resolution: "uuid@npm:11.1.0"
   bin:
@@ -36030,15 +36030,6 @@ __metadata:
   languageName: node
   linkType: hard
 
-"uuid@npm:^11.0.0, uuid@npm:^11.0.5, uuid@npm:^11.1.0":
-  version: 11.1.1
-  resolution: "uuid@npm:11.1.1"
-  bin:
-    uuid: dist/esm/bin/uuid
-  checksum: 10c0/9e3af58eba872ece5a5e76f4773a94fc78a0ef2c2444c38dbe6b42f41dadf76c01850fd783604f27986f6195e6286aef064d45987d401b2a33127b98ddf7c0c5
-  languageName: node
-  linkType: hard
-
 "uuid@npm:^13.0.0":
   version: 13.0.2
   resolution: "uuid@npm:13.0.2"
